n't  need and by the way the government being  involved in marriage is a relatively new  thing george washington was married but  he wasn't married by the government  right and yet he still had a marriage  right he just didn't have to go down to  the courthouse and fill out a piece of  paper  so when ryan and i use the term you know  spouse or wife or  marriage what we're using is a term that  describes the type of relationship that  we have it's a  a long-term partnership a long-term  commitment  now commitment is not birthed out of a  piece of paper we can go  sign a piece of paper right now and then  go cheat on the person the next day  and i don't mean cheat just in the  physical sense but cheat and all these  we can lie to them we could steal from  them we could hide things from them  these are all different ways to sort of  cheat a relationship  and so because of the the religious  aspect and the governmental aspect  you know i don't have a a formal piece  of paper but i actually have pieces of  paper that mean a lot more  to our relationship and ryan you do as  well but  i mentioned a moment ago life insurance  you know to me that's far more important  than having some sort of  you know marriage certificate uh such a  sexy topic too  life insurance i know right it's like  and  in fact because these things are so  unsexy  we almost never talk to them talk to our  significant other  about the most important things and so  i have 20-year term life insurance ryan  has the same  and that means and it's 10 times my  annual income and  so it's about 100 a month and  um maybe a little bit less and and what  that means is if i die  in the next 20 years then  bex and ella aren't going to be you know  out on the street you know  trying to figure out how they're going  to get their next meal or pay their rent  or or whatever  and i think that that is to me  one sign of commitment that has nothing  to do with just signing a piece  of paper but real commitment is birthed  